<title>JAPAN: Keisei Elec up, helped by volatile forex.</title>
<headline>Keisei Elec up, helped by volatile forex.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Keisei Electric Railway Co Ltd advanced on Monday morning as investors were drawn to issues in which trade has been somewhat speculative and volume heavy, given the volatile currency market, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0038 GMT, the issue was up 27 yen at 696. Its turnover was 1.756 million shares, making it the most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
